    "body": "> use native form validation and css :invalid selectors\n\nI would expect `:valid`/`:invalid` to be able to match `<output>` (and `<object>`) since it has a `validity.valid` state property that can be `true` or `false`, i.e. I would expect it to match depending on that state, regardless of whether it is a candidate for constraint validation and/or a submittable element. But that is probably be a separate issue.",
